{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib proof of Conjecture 377 of E. DeLaViña's \"Written on the Wall II\" (a conjecture of the computer program Graffiti.pc, posed 18 Feb 2009, status O): every tree T on n > 2 vertices satisfies γ_t(T) ≥ (number of isolates of the subgraph induced by the maximum-degree vertices) + (upper median of the degree sequence). Writing k for the number of isolated maximum-degree vertices, the proof shows γ_t ≥ k + 1 from the edge count of a tree and the bound n ≤ γ_t·Δ, and γ_t ≥ k + 2 when leaves are not a majority (upper median 2), using a Chellali–Haynes type double-counting bound for Δ ≥ 4 and an exact domination count with a short case analysis (ending in 4- or 5-cycles) for Δ = 3.",
  "authors": [
    {
      "name": "Ari Gilchrist"
    }
  ],
